## Desired behavior

AFT should be able to warn that a file/function is risky because it combines several cheap signals:
- high import fan-in or transitive dependent count;
- high complexity where available;
- large/long function or file;
- optional git churn/change count when enabled.

This is a practical approximation of Qartez hotspots.

## Scope

In scope:
- file-level hotspot-lite score;
- symbol/function-level score if complexity is already available;
- optional git churn extraction bounded by config;
- advisory integration for read/edit/write/diff.

Out of scope:
- full PageRank initially;
- full complexity trend over history;
- bus-factor/knowledge analysis;
- heavy git mining by default.
